      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hi, it’s good to meet you. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S004",
      "patient_response": "Hi, yeah, nice to meet you too. Um, well, what really pushed me to finally make this appointment is... I just keep starting these follow-up items at work. I'm an auditor, so there's always a ton of follow-up after audits, or even after these mentorship events I run. I'll sit down with every intention of finishing them. I even bought this new planner—it's got these little color-coded stickers, which I thought would help because my sister uses them and swears by them. She's a teacher, so she's always organizing something. But anyway, I'll start the task, and then days later, I find out that the final email, or the review note, or the form never actually got done. It's just sitting there, half-finished. Like, last week I was supposed to send out this summary email, and I got distracted because my cat knocked over a plant, and by the time I cleaned up the dirt, I totally forgot what I was doing. So yeah, the follow-ups just aren't getting finished.",
