    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Did you have similar trouble finishing tasks or staying focused when you were a child?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, absolutely. Even back in elementary school... I remember my report cards always said the exact same thing. They'd say I was bright, but I constantly lost my assignments, or I'd just rush past all the small details. And I talked out of turn a lot. Actually, my third-grade teacher, Mrs. Gable—she had this huge collection of ceramic frogs on her desk. Like, dozens of them. I always wondered where she bought them all, or if students just kept giving them to her as gifts, you know? Because what do you even buy a teacher? I usually just give Starbucks gift cards now. \n\nBut anyway, she was always having to remind me to finish my classwork. My mother still jokes about it to this day. She always says I could completely ace a test, but then I'd totally forget the big project just sitting right there in my backpack. It was this bright pink Lisa Frank backpack, too, with the neon dolphins. God, I loved that thing. I took it everywhere until the zipper finally broke on a family trip to Florida...",
