    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Do you get unwanted thoughts that keep intruding into your mind and feel hard to dismiss?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Unwanted thoughts? Um, no, not really. I mean, my mind is always going a mile a minute, but it's not like I'm having bad thoughts I can't get rid of. It's more just... thinking about a million things at once. Like yesterday, I was trying to reconcile this account, and suddenly I was wondering if I ever paid my water bill, which reminded me that I need to buy a new filter for the Brita pitcher. I got the pitcher on sale at Target, actually. Target's dangerous for me, I always go in for one thing and come out with a cart full of stuff I don't need. Last time I bought this throw pillow shaped like a taco. It's hilarious, but it doesn't match my couch at all. My couch is this dark grey microfiber—super easy to clean, which is great because of the cat. But yeah, no, not like scary or weird thoughts that I can't shake. Just regular thoughts, but a lot of them.",
